<task id="181" project="unified-access-control-r2">
  <metadata>
    <title>Notify an internal user, with a link to the record, when they are given access (a grant to an internal-linked contact, or a user share), and replace the dev-facing "Internal notify … escalated" notice (owner round 89 item 3)</title>
    <phase>Session 28 — UAC (owner round 89, 2026-10-09)</phase>
    <status>pending</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>New server behaviour on the grant and share paths plus a modal change; modifies tests.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Touches grant and share routes and the shared AccessGrantModal; must be best-effort and never fail a grant.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Edits AccessGrantModal and the TrackingFieldTrio bundle (also edited by 175) and the grant/share endpoints. Start after 175 merges; coordinate with 179 (same route group) by merge order.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>175</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, pcf, react, testing, deploy</tags>
    <estimated-effort>1 day</estimated-effort>
    <origin>Owner round 89 item 3 ("Build it now"). AccessGrantModal.tsx (around :1290-1300) sets notifyPending for internal contacts and shows "Internal notify (deep-link) is not yet available for internal workforce contacts (escalated; see project notes)".</origin>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Implement round 89 item 3: when an internal user is given access to a record, they receive a notification that links to the record. Replace the dev-facing notice with user-facing wording.</prompt>

  <goal>(1) WHO. A grant to a contact linked to an internal user (the existing isInternalContact classification and its server-side equivalent), and an internal user share (+User / share-user). The notification goes to that internal user. It is not sent to the person granting access, and it is not sent when nothing changed (re-share at the same level).
(2) HOW. Reuse task 100's in-app notification mechanism (Dataverse appnotification with a deep link to the record; see notes/task-100-expiry-reminders.md and its code) from the SERVER side, after the grant or share write succeeds. Best effort: a failed notification never fails or rolls back the grant, and is logged. No new channel unless the design shows the in-app notification cannot reach the user; in that case STOP and report.
(3) TEXT. Plain wording, for example: title "You were given access to {record type} {record name}", body "{granter} gave you {level} access." Linked to the record. The record name is read app-only only after the grant succeeded, so nothing leaks to someone without access.
(4) MODAL. Remove notifyPending's dev message. On success show "Granted access to N item(s)." plus the narrowed note when it applies. If the server reports that a notification could not be sent, add "Some people could not be notified; share the record link with them."
(5) Version bumps for TrackingFieldTrio (all 5 locations) if its bundle changes.</goal>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §11">Reuse task 100's notifier; justify any new surface.</constraint>
    <constraint source="security">The notification never names a record to someone who was not just granted access to it.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>projects/unified-access-control-r2/notes/task-100-expiry-reminders.md</file>
      <file>src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/AccessGrantModal/AccessGrantModal.tsx</file>
      <file>docs/guides/PCF-DEPLOYMENT-GUIDE.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step>Find task 100's notifier, wire it into the grant and share success paths for internal recipients, update the modal, add tests, open the PR.</step>
  </steps>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion>A grant to an internal-linked contact and an internal user share each create one notification for that user, linked to the record (one test each).</criterion>
    <criterion>A notification failure leaves the grant in place and is reported in the response (one test).</criterion>
    <criterion>A re-share at the same level does not notify. An external grant does not trigger this path (CIAM email is unchanged).</criterion>
    <criterion>The modal no longer shows "escalated; see project notes" (jest).</criterion>
    <criterion>Test scope: the cases named above. Anything beyond that needs a one-line justification.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>
</task>
